# Graphify (smart)

Only when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists.

## Use graphify first when

- You do not already know the files/symbols for a codebase or architecture question
- You need relationships: what calls X, path from A to B, impact of changing Y
- A subagent will explore the repo (put these rules in its prompt)

## Skip graphify when

- The user named the file/symbol, or you already have the exact path from this session
- Pure copy, docs, commit, PR, or deploy with no code discovery
- Fixing a known line/lint after orientation already happened this session

## How to query (keeps tokens low)

Prefer in this order:

1. `graphify explain "<SymbolOrFile>"` — neighbors of one concept
2. `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — shortest dependency path
3. `graphify query "<specific symbols>" --context call --budget 2500`

Do **not**:

- Broad English questions on large apps (pulls UI hubs like Button/cn/Avatar)
- Read all of `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` or `GRAPH_REPORT.md` by default
- Prefer `graphify-out/AGENT_NAV.md` (short) if present; open one community wiki page only when needed

After orientation, Read/Grep only the few files you will edit or verify. After substantive code edits: `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).
